						{ label: 'Florida\'s terminology', body: 'The plan should say "time-sharing," not "visitation" or "custody." It should say "Parenting Plan," not "custody agreement." Courts notice when out-of-state or AI-generated templates use the wrong vocabulary.' },
						{ label: '2023 presumption addressed', body: 'If your plan proposes anything other than 50/50, include a brief factual basis. Courts are more likely to approve an unequal arrangement when the plan itself explains the reasoning (distance, age, work schedule, documented concerns).' },
